    {
      "contentTypeKey": "3ef5c851-77d2-46af-9a22-e2bfadd01829",
      "udi": "umb://element/de7aef486bf5422ea945d561c1e1b9ea",
      "title": "Mix Designs",
      "content": "<p>The PI section of a soil laboratory assesses physical and chemical properties.</p>\n<p>This includes more delicate testing to determine moisture, plasticity, material classification and more.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Why perform PI testing?<br /></strong>Known as Atterberg Limits, these are key indicators of soil behavior under different moisture conditions.</p>\n<p>By determining the shrinkage limit, liquid limit, plastic limit and plasticity index, professionals gain insights into how the soil will behave under varying moisture conditions.</p>\n<p>Understanding moisture characteristics is crucial for compaction control, slope stability analysis and overall project planning, and is very commonly used in road construction.</p>",
      "images": [
        {
          "key": "9a989a8c-d0dd-494f-9377-272b2c733427",
